locations can be added later through Locations.</p><h3 id="help-section-1">Permissions</h3><p>Browser creation/import needs <strong>Builders &amp; imports → Build and import inventory structures</strong> together with its inventory dependency. An administrator can grant that capability to a Technician or Supervisor without making the person an administrator. View inventory, Add and edit items, Move items, Run stock verifications and Export reports remain separate permissions.</p><p>By default, technicians can view inventory and check stock; supervisors can also add/edit and move items. Administrators have full access. Department membership is not a substitute for an application permission.</p></section><section id="ui107-boxes-and-contents"><h2 id="help-review-boxes-and-their-contents-before-import">Review boxes and their contents before import</h2><p>After mapping an inventory worksheet, open <strong>Boxes and contents</strong>. Review each included row's asset/tag reference, explicit box flag, parent box reference and expected quantity. Searching, paging and opening this view do not change the checked proposal. Editing a field requires checking the changed draft again.</p><p>A parent must be an included, explicitly marked box with a unique asset/tag reference in the <strong>same worksheet</strong>. Use its exact reference, including leading zeros and punctuation, or choose <strong>No container</strong> deliberately. A name, serial number, part number, indentation or the word BOX does not establish a relationship. References across worksheets or to boxes already in the destination inventory are not resolved during this import.</p><p>Review missing or excluded parents, duplicate references, self-links, cycles and excessive depth. A box describes one container; use an expected quantity of one or leave it Unknown when appropriate. Ordinary stock can have zero or another valid expected quantity. No imported quantity is a completed stock verification.</p><p>Contained rows inherit their top box's effective location. The checked import summary uses that location before saving, and a differing mapped location is retained in Notes. Review this together with worksheet locations. A location note records the reviewed mapping; it is not proof of a physical move.</p><p>Explicit parent and box-flag headers help suggest inventory. Unqualified Box/Container ID or reference headers can identify the row itself or its parent, so map them deliberately as an asset/tag or parent reference. Unmapped source columns remain available as source notes.</p><p>Field edits keep full mapped row order, original row references when available and item choices. Reapplying a mapping replaces the mapped values and these corrections; editing the complete table can reset source references and choices. Review the visible notice before continuing. Pending or uncertain saves must retain their unchanged retry request.</p></section><section id="ui108-inventory-source-review"><h2 id="help-review-source-rows-and-header-choices">Review source rows and header choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, use <strong>Needs source review</strong> to inspect rows that resemble repeated headers, headings, summaries, instructions or footers. The advice describes the original extracted source. Rows remain included until you deliberately exclude them. Items can legitimately be called Total or Instructions; compare their identifiers and expected quantities with the source.</p><p>The header selector includes the first 250 extracted nonempty rows. Open <strong>Find header row</strong> to search and page through any extracted row, compare its preview, and choose the actual column header. Original Excel row labels appear only when the extractor proves them. Review any notice about rows before the selected header or other header candidates. Changing the header requires applying the mapping and checking the changed proposal again.</p><p>Editing the complete raw table clears source-row advice and provenance when they can no longer be established. Field corrections keep their original-source references, but do not turn the original advice into a statement about the corrected item. Source Counted columns remain Notes; the app performs stock verification.</p></section><section id="ui109-inventory-item-corrections"><h2 id="help-correct-one-imported-item-without-resetting-choices">Correct one imported item without resetting choices</h2><p>In <strong>Choose items</strong>, open <strong>Edit item</strong> to correct that row's <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Serial number (SN)</strong> or <strong>Part number (PN)</strong>. Apply a real change, then <strong>Check</strong> the proposal again. Cancel or an unchanged Apply retains the existing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships.</p><p>Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains.</p></section><p id="ui111-inventory-review-safeguards"><strong>Keep corrections while reviewing worksheets.</strong> Switching <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> only changes the worksheet you are inspecting. A completed check, its import overview and your confirmation stay available. Changing included sheets, locations, destination or item fields still requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again. Before <strong>Apply mapping</strong> replaces manually corrected names, SN/PN, quantities or box relationships, review the warning for that worksheet. Cancel keeps the corrected rows. Confirm replaces corrections for that worksheet with mapped source values and requires another check. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal.</p><p id="ui112-inventory-review-navigation"><strong>Navigate the inventory review.</strong> <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> and each worksheet’s <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> button change only the sheet on screen. <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping.</p></article>
