t low-stock alerts</a><a href="qrverification.html">Scan labels during stock verification</a><a href="fleet.html">Manage vessels and shore bases</a><a href="fleetaccess.html">Set vessel-only access</a><a href="manifests.html">Dispatch and receive with manifests</a><a href="receiving.html">Receive equipment and record final placement</a><a href="itemjourney.html">Follow an item’s journey</a><a href="vessellogs.html">Use vessel-specific logbooks</a><a href="vessellogaccess.html">Set vessel log permissions</a><a href="browseradmin.html">Browser administration and navigation</a><a href="accessreview.html">Review effective access and sensitive backups</a><a href="browsertemplates.html">Browser checklist and maintenance authoring</a><a href="browsertoolbox.html">Browser toolbox-talk form authoring</a><a href="browserlogs.html">Design logbooks in the browser</a></details><a href="handovers.html">Handovers: private drafts and revisions</a><a href="handovercontinuity.html">Prepare handovers &amp; current recipients</a></nav><div class="content"><section class="chapter" data-topic="inventorybuilder" id="inventorybuilder"><p class="kicker">User instructions</p><h1>Build an inventory</h1><p><strong>Import document items into one inventory.</strong> Choose a workbook from Setup &amp; builders, select the item worksheets, then review each mapping and its location. All selected sheets save into one new inventory. To add items to a saved inventory, choose Add to existing inventory or use its Import items action. Check again after changing included sheets, mapped rows, locations or the destination. Browsing another worksheet keeps the completed check. Builder, inventory-view and item-edit permissions are needed to add items.</p><p class="subtitle">Create the structure before entering stock</p><h2>Browser inventory builder</h2>
 <p>Use <strong>Inventory &amp; boxes → Create inventory / Import existing</strong>, or <strong>Setup &amp; builders → Inventory structure</strong>. Creation defines an empty list and locations. Import existing reviews a supported .ajinventory package before saving; document item imports use the separate <strong>Import a document</strong> flow above.</p>
